<title>FRANCE: CGE sees 1997 net at over four bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>CGE sees 1997 net at over four bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The net attributable profit of Generale des Eaux should be higher than four billion francs in 1997, chairman Jean-Marie Messier told an analysts' meeting.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the company confirmed the figure but added it had already been given at previous meetings.</p>
<p>Messier added that Generale des Eaux would make a asset gain of over two billion francs in 1997 on the operation with Havas in which it will take a 30 percent stake and sell its 19.3 percent stake in Canal Plus.</p>
<p>Messier told analysts that the gain would be &quot;closer to 2.5 billion francs than to two billion.&quot;</p>
</text>
